{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden corpus for the release-name parser. Each case asserts only the",
    "fields it lists: an absent field is not checked, which keeps a case",
    "focused on the behaviour it exists to pin down.",
    "",
    "Cases marked pathological:true document names the parser gets WRONG or",
    "cannot fully resolve. Their expectations are the current, accepted",
    "behaviour, so the corpus is a regression lock rather than a wish list.",
    "Changing one of those expectations should be a deliberate decision.",
    "",
    "Names tagged 'apibay' are shapes the live Pirate Bay JSON API actually",
    "returns: dots flattened to spaces, and the name field cut at 80 chars."
  ],
